{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Vision-Language Models \u2014 The ViT-MLP-LLM Pattern Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: The projector"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The part you will train most often. 2-4 layer MLP with GELU."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch.nn as nn"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class Projector(nn.Module):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, vit_dim=768, llm_dim=4096, hidden=4096):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        super().__init__()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.net = nn.Sequential("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.Linear(vit_dim, hidden),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.GELU(),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.Linear(hidden, llm_dim),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def forward(self, x):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return self.net(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Input is a `(N_patches, d_vit)` token tensor. Output is `(N_patches, d_llm)`. The LLM treats every output row as just another token."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: Assemble ViT-MLP-LLM end-to-end"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Skeleton of the forward pass for a minimal VLM. Real code uses `transformers`; this is the conceptual layout."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class MinimalVLM(nn.Module):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, vit, projector, llm, image_token_id):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        super().__init__()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.vit = vit"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.projector = projector"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.llm = llm"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.image_token_id = image_token_id  # placeholder token in text prompt"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def forward(self, image, input_ids, attention_mask):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        # 1. vision features"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        vision_tokens = self.vit(image)                     # (B, N_patches, d_vit)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        vision_embeds = self.projector(vision_tokens)       # (B, N_patches, d_llm)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        # 2. text embeddings"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        text_embeds = self.llm.get_input_embeddings()(input_ids)  # (B, M, d_llm)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        # 3. replace image placeholder tokens with vision embeds"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        merged = self._merge(text_embeds, vision_embeds, input_ids)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        # 4. run LLM"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return self.llm(inputs_embeds=merged, attention_mask=attention_mask)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def _merge(self, text_embeds, vision_embeds, input_ids):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        out = text_embeds.clone()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        expected = vision_embeds.size(1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for b in range(input_ids.size(0)):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            positions = (input_ids[b] == self.image_token_id).nonzero(as_tuple=True)[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            if len(positions) != expected:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                raise ValueError("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                    f\"batch item {b} has {len(positions)} image tokens but vision_embeds has {expected} patches.\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                    \" Every sample in the batch must be pre-padded to the same number of image placeholder tokens.\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            out[b, positions] = vision_embeds[b]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return out"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The `<image>` placeholder token in the text gets replaced with real image embeddings \u2014 same pattern LLaVA, Qwen-VL, and InternVL use."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: CMER computation"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "A lightweight runtime check."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch.nn.functional as F"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def cross_modal_error_rate(image_emb, text_emb, text_confidence, sim_threshold=0.25, conf_threshold=0.8):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"\"\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    image_emb, text_emb: embeddings of image and generated text (normalised internally)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    text_confidence:     mean per-token probability in [0, 1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    Returns:             fraction of high-confidence outputs with low image-text alignment"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"\"\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    image_emb = F.normalize(image_emb, dim=-1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    text_emb = F.normalize(text_emb, dim=-1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    sim = (image_emb * text_emb).sum(dim=-1)        # cosine similarity"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    high_conf_low_sim = (text_confidence > conf_threshold) & (sim < sim_threshold)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return high_conf_low_sim.float().mean().item()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Treat CMER as a production KPI. Monitor it per endpoint, per prompt type, per customer. Rising CMER indicates the model is starting to hallucinate on some input distribution."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: Toy VLM classifier (runnable)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Demonstrate the projector trains. Fake \"ViT features\" go in; a tiny LLM-style token predicts a class."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class ToyVLM(nn.Module):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, vit_dim=32, llm_dim=64, num_classes=5):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        super().__init__()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.projector = Projector(vit_dim, llm_dim, hidden=64)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.head = nn.Linear(llm_dim, num_classes)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def forward(self, vision_tokens):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        projected = self.projector(vision_tokens)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        pooled = projected.mean(dim=1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return self.head(pooled)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "One can fit this on synthetic (feature, class) pairs in under 200 steps \u2014 enough to show the projector pattern works."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **(Easy)** Run three prompts (\"what is this?\", \"count the objects\", \"describe the scene\") through any open VLM on five images. Score each answer as correct / partially correct / hallucinated by hand. Compute a first-pass CMER-like rate.\n2. **(Medium)** Fine-tune Qwen2.5-VL-3B or LLaVA-1.6-7B with LoRA (rank 16) on 500 images of a target domain with captions. Compare zero-shot vs fine-tuned MMBench-style accuracy.\n3. **(Hard)** Replace the VLM's image encoder with DINOv3 instead of its default SigLIP/CLIP. Re-train only the projector (frozen LLM + frozen DINOv3). Measure whether dense-prediction tasks (counting, spatial reasoning) improve."
      ]
    }
